    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-16766" textLabel="MONOMER-16766" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-16766" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="1050" centerY="1075" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang">Conversion of a xenobiotic (fenclorim) cysteine-S-conjugate to its corresponding S-methylated xenobiotic was detected in extracts from Arabidopsis cell suspension culture in a protein-dependent manner, in the presence of SAM. No thiol intermediate was detected suggesting that the C-S lyase and methyltransferase must act in a closely coordinated manner in the conversion. The combined enzyme activities were greatly enhanced in cells treated with fenclorim |CITS: [18522943]|. No gene has been identified for either of the enzyme activity.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-16766" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-19413" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18522943" />
    </DataNode>
